Package: nlmixr2bayes
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Interface for 'nlmixr2'
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matthew L.", "Fidler", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "matthew.fidler@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8538-6691")),
    person("Lukas A.", "Widmer", role="aut"))
Description: Bayesian estimation for 'nlmixr2' models by linking Stan (via
    'rstan') directly to the compiled 'rxode2'/'nlmixr2est' likelihoods rather
    than re-expressing the model in the Stan language.  The ordinary
    differential equation solving, residual-error models and censoring stay in
    one place ('rxode2'/'nlmixr2est'), and Stan consumes the likelihood and its
    analytically-supplied gradients as an external function.  Prior
    distributions come from the model's 'ini({})' block, whose distribution
    catalogue is one-to-one with Stan's.
